{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>Whether the cry that has come to Me.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat), the explanation of the verse is as its Targum: 'Whether the cry that has come to Me — they are guilty of destruction'; this is what it says: כלה. 'And if they do not repent, I will punish them'; this is: ואם לא תייבין אתפרע. And he made the word אדעה from the language of (Judges 8:16): ״ויודע בהם את אנשי סכות״. (Psalms 138:6): ״וגבוה ממרחק יידע״." "<b>By way of the Midrash.</b> הכצעקתה — it is not written הכצעקתם here, but rather הכצעקתה, and which one? This is the cry of the woman rival, in Bereshit Rabbah." "<b>By way of the Kabbalah.</b> <b>Whether the cry that has come to Me</b> — the men of Sodom denied the distinctive Name, like the men of the city and the tower, and therefore it is written here ״וירד ה׳״, and here ״ארדה נא״, for He showed them His power. And Scripture says: I will go down from the attribute of mercy to the attribute of judgment, ״ואראה״ — in mercy, as in the mystery of (Exodus 2): ״וירא אלהים את בני ישראל״. הכצעקתה, that is, the cry of the ה״א that comes to Me in the attribute of judgment — they acted; I will consume them all in the attribute of judgment. ואם לא אדעה, that is, I will draw down into the Da'at, as in the mystery of ״וידע אלהים״. The sense of the verse is (Exodus 3): ״הנה צעקת בני ישראל באה אלי״ — that it cries out before the King, YHWH, from amid the great distress with which the Egyptians oppress them."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {2 "Citations '(שמות ב)' and '(שמות ג)' normalized to Exodus 2:25 and Exodus 3:9 respectively; the וידע אלהים allusion is to Exodus 2:25."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:13:29.358295401Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}